    "result": "I implemented `shipping_cost` in `solution.py` and wrote a pytest suite in `tests/test_solution.py`. `python -m pytest -q tests` reports 73 passed. I did not measure line coverage, since the only shell command allowed was the test run. The tests exercise every branch of `solution.py`, so coverage should clear the 90% gate, but that is unverified.\n\nThe implementation converts inputs to `Decimal`, using `str()` for floats. It rejects `bool` and non-numeric types with `TypeError`, and rejects non-finite values with `ValueError`. Zone must be the `int` 1, 2 or 3, and any other zone value raises `ValueError`. Billable weight is the larger of actual and volumetric weight, rounded up to a 0.5 kg step. The base charge is 8.00 plus 1.50 per further half kilogram, then multiplied by the zone factor. Free shipping (subtotal ≥ 150 in zones 1 and 2) zeroes the base charge only. The oversize surcharge of 12.00 applies when the longest side is over 120 cm and is added after the zone factor and free-shipping step. The total is quantized to cents with `ROUND_HALF_UP` at the end. Two choices go beyond the spec: non-finite numbers (NaN, infinity) raise `ValueError`, and the type check runs before the value checks.",
